    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0095" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/769</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-08T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                                1917, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your cipher telegram of December 6, 7 p.m. The American Government supports the
                    view that China is entirely within her right in employing troops to protect her
                    sovereignty and territorial integrity. This Government would not, however, be
                    disposed to encourage an armed conflict.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
